            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_83fbafc7">
               <extent xml:id="extent_49e024ef">14 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_4908480a">26.5 x 34.5</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_d4b61911">Written in pencil. Paper: 14 staves. Beneath a sketch for "Saa mange i Tal de ere" (HartW A 14) from Berthold Auerbachs "I stille Timer". Beside the first bar Hartmann has written: "Historiske Sange pag 74", referring to H. Nutzhorn's and L. Schrøder's collection "Historiske Sange" which was published in 1872. Title between staves 7 and 8; and text fragment "krum paa Skiold med Sværdet i sit Hierte" between staves 10 and 11. Differs from the draft in Hartmanns Samling 073.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
            <notesStmt xml:id="notesStmt_4fa5a510">
               <annot type="source_description" xml:id="annot_9a236eb2">
                  <p xml:id="idm35">On the first page of a gathering containing sketches for Acts One and Two and Finale of "Arcona" (HartW 9).</p>
               </annot>
            </notesStmt>
